<h2>When every step becomes uncomfortable</h2>
<p><b>At first, it’s often just a slight tugging sensation.</b></p>
<p>Then come the moments when you suddenly feel your knee more acutely:</p>
<ul><li>Standing up</li><li>On stairs</li><li>Sitting for a long time</li><li>Walking or standing for extended periods</li></ul>
<p>Many people automatically start to avoid certain movements. They walk more slowly, unconsciously take the weight off their knee, or feel unsteady during everyday movements.</p>
<p><b>The problem is this: the more carefully you move, the more your knee becomes the focus of your daily life.</b></p>
</div>
