<h2>Maybe it's not just wear and tear</h2>
<p>Many conventional explanations focus solely on “wear and tear.”</p>
<p>However, knee pain often feels more like pressure, irritation, or instability.</p>
<p><b>One possible cause may be irritated synovial tissue</b>—the sensitive lining of the knee joint. When this tissue becomes irritated, <b>the knee may react more sensitively to stress.</b></p>
<p>This can manifest as:</p>
<ul><li>A feeling of pressure around the kneecap</li><li>Stiffness after periods of rest</li><li>Uncertainty during movement</li><li>Sensitivity under stress</li></ul>
<p>Many conventional knee braces attempt to solve the problem with rigid stability. <b>However, hard braces can be uncomfortable, slip out of place, or restrict natural movement.</b></p>
<p>That is exactly why Peakflex was designed differently.</p>
